{"id":"01a046af-90be-7c96-bd3e-870ece00b5ed","issue_id":"project-LICHEN-worker6-x6op.8","event_type":"closed","actor":"Mark Atwood","old_value":"","new_value":"Already fixed. The concern about partial encryption state is mitigated by: (1) SecretVec implements ZeroizeOnDrop - any partial data is zeroized when dropped on error, (2) session is poison()ed on error preventing reuse, (3) ciphertext_3 is a local variable not stored in session state. Security audit commit 7434512 specifically fixed 'Replace empty ZeroizeOnDrop impls with proper Drop calling zeroize()' which addresses this concern.","created_at":"2026-08-28T04:45:06.110827Z"}
